t **no numpy/scipy/torch/jax/gym installed** and cannot be downloaded. Consequences/fallbacks:\n- If the canonical DRL training requires torch/jax, it is infeasible HERE unless dependencies are pre-bundled/offline \u2014 the design therefore ASSUMES a lightweight, self-contained environment (or an offline-bundled stack / external compute grant). A pragmatic fallback is a pure-Python/NumPy-free (stdlib) implementation or a scripted-policy rollout comparison on a fixed seed grid, with explicitly reduced inferential scope.\n- Primary evaluation (8\u00d710\u2076 env steps) is trivially parallelizable across the 224 cores.\n- High-censoring risk (many agents surviving H) \u2192 power for the raw mean is bounded; mitigated by the survival analysis and by choosing T so that typical agents die within H under ON (calibrated in Phase 0).\n- **No experiment has been run; this document is the design only.**\n\n## 6. Deliverables\nPre-registered protocol; parameter pinning report (Phase 0 sanity); training attainment table; results table (\u03b4, \u0394_H, \u0394_N, each with 95% CI, effect sizes, CIs); Kaplan\u2013Meier/Cox output; robustness-arm table; code + seed/parameter manifest; statement of deviations from protocol.", "assumptions": ["ALL numeric parameters (H, T, W, pirate hp/damage, radius, K for recurring variant, death rule threshold) are unverified defaults to be confirmed in Phase 0 \u2014 they are not sourced from any document.", "Survival duration = whole-episode steps alive, threshold-inclusive, censored at H; the primary endpoint is fixed as such.", "Hierarchical = two-level manager/worker (subgoal at coarse timescale) and non-hierarchical = flat policy, with matched parameters, steps, and obs/action/reward interface; training regime fixed to mechanic-ON with a common criterion.", "Invasion triggering is per-episode, deterministic, and identical across architectures at fixed T; any architecture difference in WHEN it fires (via scoring rate) is a covariate to control, not a design defect.", "Per-protocol (reached-threshold) is the primary population; ITT and share-reaching-threshold are reported alongside so the exclusion is transparent.", "A compute/runtime budget sufficient to train at least ~10 seeds per architecture on a lightweight environment is available; this is NOT stated in the task and is the largest resource assumption.", "Sizing is pilot-gated (\u03c3_b\u00b2, \u03c3_w\u00b2 unknown until Phase 0); no fixed power claim is made a priori."], "uncertainties": ["Exact mechanic spec (T, wave strength, damage, timing, one-shot vs recurring) has no source in this workspace; defaults must be confirmed by the task owner.", "Whether the intended 'survival duration' includes time after the threshold; the design fixes threshold-inclusive whole-episode D as primary and reports post-threshold D_after separately so the definition can be switched without re-running.", "Whether invasion triggering differs by architecture through differing scoring rates; mitigated (\u03c4 covariate, matched subsample, phase-aligned analysis) but not eliminable.", "Whether every agent/episode faces the invasion depends on crossing T; structurally excluded episodes are handled via per-protocol/ITT reporting and attainment metric.", "Dependency/runtime feasibility: network is disabled and no ML/science packages are installed, so DRL training may be infeasible in this sandbox; the design assumes a lightweight env or offline-bundled/ external compute.", "Censoring rate at H and between-seed variance are unknown until pilot, so final achievable power and effect size are pilot-gated.", "Direction of the interaction (does invasion widen/shrink/reverse the H\u2013N gap) is not assumed; the experiment estimates it."], "evidence": "Repository/workspace observations: /workspace contains only task.json (482 B); its \"documents.track.md\" is a stub string (\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\") and no such file exists. Filesystem-wide searches for track/pirate/craft artifacts returned only unrelated system files (cursor themes, nodejs pirates package, pygments minecraft lexer, kernel headers). Environment: Python 3.14.4 with pip 25.1.1, but numpy/scipy/torch/jax/gym absent and network disabled \u2192 DRL training cannot be installed in this sandbox; nproc=224, gpu_enabled=false, datasets=[]. Feasible checks confirming the design: env-step math (primary 800 eval episodes \u2248 8e6 steps, trivial on 224 cores) and per-phase sanity checks in Phase 0; power-solver is pilot-gated from \u03c3_b\u00b2/\u03c3_w\u00b2; paired difference-in-differences \u03b4 = \u0394_H \u2212 \u0394_N with mixed-effects interaction and Cox hazard interaction is the standard, pre-registrable way to answer an effect-modification question; per-protocol/ITT + \u03c4-covariate + phase-aligned analysis specifically neutralizes the architecture-dependent-trigger-timing confound identified in the task. Rationale for every control and each statistical choice is given in the design document (sections 3\u20135). No experiment executed; outcome not fabricated."}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-8f2a7c570fa2484e9fd06876c061b402", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "Deliver complete experiment design document for invasion x architecture survival study", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
